{
  "task": {
    "id": "Prob078_dualedge",
    "spec": "\r\nI would like you to implement a module named TopModule with the following\r\ninterface. All input and output ports are one bit unless otherwise\r\nspecified.\r\n\r\n - input  clk\r\n - input  d\r\n - output q\r\n\r\nA dual-edge triggered flip-flop is triggered on both edges of the clock.\r\nHowever, FPGAs don't have dual-edge triggered flip-flops, and using an\r\nalways @(posedge clk or negedge clk) is not accepted as a legal\r\nsensitivity list. Build a circuit that functionally behaves like a\r\ndual-edge triggered flip-flop.\r\n\r\n",
    "interface": {
      "top": "TopModule",
      "ports": [
        {
          "name": "clk",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "d",
          "direction": "input",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        },
        {
          "name": "q",
          "direction": "output",
          "width": 1,
          "signed": false
        }
      ]
    },
    "constraints": "SystemVerilog, single self-contained TopModule DUT; xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; 5 ns synthesis clock; simulator seed 1. No reference dependencies, hierarchy outside the DUT, file access, includes or DPI."
  },
  "sample_id": "4ad01bb7-753f-4bed-9e0d-bf9aae066a82",
  "variant_id": "C",
  "current": {
    "revision_id": "145fa260-893e-4f3f-bac4-36f6ff5d4cf8",
    "source_sha256": "83198f705a714fc9eb0a77fb0eece8261ed4e3da321b1f90444c6c7f5f3edbe0",
    "source": "module TopModule(\n    input  logic clk,\n    input  logic d,\n    output logic q\n);\n\n    // Two single-edge registers whose XOR reproduces dual-edge behavior\n    // without any clock-level mux (which would glitch at every clock edge).\n    logic p = 1'b0;\n    logic n = 1'b0;\n\n    // Positive-edge triggered storage\n    always_ff @(posedge clk)\n        p <= d ^ n;\n\n    // Negative-edge triggered storage\n    always_ff @(negedge clk)\n        n <= d ^ p;\n\n    // q reflects d after either edge:\n    //   posedge: p^n -> (d^n)^n = d\n    //   negedge: p^n -> p^(d^p) = d\n    assign q = p ^ n;\n\nendmodule\n"
  },
